[2026-03-14T19:42:00.761Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0196fhcxKPH14Uh6VT3BPck4","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Google Flights App - Complete Exploration Summary\n\n### 1. App Directory Name\n- **Location**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights`\n\n### 2. Test Files (*.spec.ts)\nLocated in `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/`:\n- `airport-autocomplete.spec.ts`\n- `cabin-class-selector.spec.ts`\n- `date-picker.spec.ts`\n- `passenger-count-selector.spec.ts`\n- `popular-destinations.spec.ts`\n- `recent-searches.spec.ts`\n- `search-button.spec.ts`\n- `trip-type-selector.spec.ts`\n\n### 3. Test Documentation\n- **File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/docs/tests.md`\n- **Content**: Comprehensive test specifications for all components across the application\n\n### 4. SearchSummaryBar Component\n\n**Location**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/SearchSummaryBar.tsx`\n\n**Purpose**: Displays search parameters on the results page and allows inline editing of each parameter.\n\n**Props Interface**:\n```typescript\ninterface SearchSummaryBarProps {\n  origin: string\n  destination: string\n  departureDate: string\n  returnDate: string | null\n  tripType: string\n  cabinClass: string\n  adults: number\n  children: number\n  infants: number\n  onSearch: (params: {...}) => void\n}\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Displays origin, destination, dates (single or range), passenger count, and cabin class as clickable chips\n- Inline editing with dropdown/autocomplete editors for each chip\n- Click-outside detection to close editors without changes\n- Uses component state to track which field is being edited\n- Related components: `AirportAutocomplete`, `DatePicker`, `PassengerCountSelector`, `CabinClassSelector`\n\n**Test Specifications** (from docs/tests.md):\n1. **SearchSummaryBar displays search parameters after search** - Shows all parameters (LAX → JFK, dates, passengers, cabin class) inline and clickable\n2. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit origin airport** - Click origin, autocomplete editor opens, type and select airport, search re-executes\n3. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit destination airport** - Click destination, editor opens, select new airport, results update\n4. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit departure date** - Click departure date, date picker opens, select new date, search re-executes\n5. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit return date** - Click return date, date picker opens, select new date for round trip\n6. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit passengers** - Click passenger count, selector opens, adjust counts (adults/children/infants)\n7. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit cabin class** - Click cabin class, dropdown shows options (Economy, Premium Economy, Business, First), selection triggers re-search\n8. **SearchSummaryBar inline editor closes without changes on outside click** - Clicking outside editor closes it without updating parameters\n9. **SearchSummaryBar can be edited multiple times in sequence** - Each edit triggers a new search; summary reflects all changes\n\n### 5. TrackPricesToggle Component\n\n**Location**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TrackPricesToggle.tsx`\n\n**Purpose**: Toggle button to enable/disable price tracking for a specific flight route.\n\n**Props Interface**:\n```typescript\ninterface TrackPricesToggleProps {\n  originCode: string\n  destCode: string\n  departureDate: string\n  returnDate: string | null\n  cabinClass: string\n}\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Displays toggle button with icon (🔔 when tracked, 🔕 when not)\n- Button text changes: \"Tracking prices\" (on) / \"Track prices\" (off)\n- Dispatches `toggleTrackRoute` Redux action from `flightsSlice`\n- Reads `isTracked` and `isTrackedLoading` from Redux state\n- Uses session token from `searchSlice`\n- Handles loading state during API calls\n\n**Test Specifications** (from docs/tests.md):\n1. **TrackPricesToggle is displayed on results page** - \"Track prices\" toggle visible, initially in off/untracked state\n2. **TrackPricesToggle enables price tracking** - Toggle switches to on state, route saved to database for session\n3. **TrackPricesToggle disables price tracking** - Toggle switches to off state, route removed from tracked_routes database\n4. **TrackPricesToggle reflects existing tracked route** - If route previously tracked, toggle shows on state when user searches same route again\n5. **TrackPricesToggle tracked route appears in My Trips** - Tracked route appears in \"Tracked\" tab of My Trips page with details\n6. **TrackPricesToggle can be toggled multiple times** - Multiple toggles work correctly; database updates on each toggle\n\n### 6. Playwright Configuration\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/playwright.config.ts`\n\n**Key Settings**:\n- **Test directory**: `./tests`\n- **Timeout**: 60 seconds per test\n- **Assertion timeout**: 10 seconds\n- **Parallel execution**: Disabled (fullyParallel: false)\n- **Workers**: 1\n- **Retries**: 0\n- **Reporter**: List format and JSON output to `test-results/results.json`\n- **Base URL**: `http://localhost:8888`\n- **Tracing**: on-first-retry\n- **Browser**: Replay-enabled Chromium\n- **Web Server**: Netlify dev server on port 8888\n\n### 7. Test Helpers and Fixtures\n\n**Location**: Inline in test files (example from `search-button.spec.ts`)\n\n**Key Helper Function**: `fillSearchForm()`\n- Fills a valid search form with origin, destination, and dates\n- Options support:\n  - `skipOrigin`, `skipDestination`, `skipDepartureDate`, `skipReturnDate`\n  - `oneWay` flag to select One Way trip type\n- Uses test IDs to interact with form fields\n- Includes error handling and wait conditions (e.g., waiting for dropdowns)\n- Example: Types airport codes (LAX for Los Angeles, JFK for New York), selects from suggestions\n\n**Pattern Used**: Test IDs follow naming convention like:\n- `trip-type-selector-trigger`\n- `origin-input`, `origin-dropdown`, `origin-suggestion-{CODE}`\n- `departure-date-trigger`, `departure-date-calendar`\n\n### 8. Redux Store/Slices\n\n**Store Location**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/store.ts`\n\n**Configured Reducers**:\n- `search` - searchSlice reducer\n- `flights` - flightsSlice reducer\n- `booking` - bookingSlice reducer\n- `trips` - tripsSlice reducer\n- `explore` - exploreSlice reducer\n\n#### **searchSlice** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/searchSlice.ts`)\n\n**State Interface**:\n```typescript\ninterface SearchState {\n  tripType: TripType  // 'round_trip' | 'one_way' | 'multi_city'\n  passengers: { adults: number; children: number; infants: number }\n  cabinClass: CabinClass  // 'economy' | 'premium_economy' | 'business' | 'first'\n  origin: Airport | null\n  destination: Airport | null\n  departureDate: string | null\n  returnDate: string | null\n  recentSearches: RecentSearch[]\n  recentSearchesLoading: boolean\n  popularDestinations: PopularDestination[]\n  popularDestinationsLoading: boolean\n  sessionToken: string\n  validationErrors: Record<string, string>\n}\n```\n\n**Key Actions**:\n- `setTripType` - Updates trip type; clears returnDate if one_way\n- `setPassengers` - Updates passenger counts\n- `setCabinClass` - Updates cabin class\n- `setOrigin`, `setDestination` - Sets airport; clears validation errors\n- `swapAirports` - Exchanges origin and destination\n- `setDepartureDate`, `setReturnDate` - Sets dates; clears validation errors\n- `setValidationErrors`, `clearValidationErrors` - Manages validation state\n\n**Async Thunks**:\n- `fetchRecentSearches` - Fetches recent searches for session\n- `saveRecentSearch` - Saves a new search\n- `fetchPopularDestinations` - Fetches popular destinations\n\n**Session Management**:\n- `sessionToken` is auto-generated with `crypto.randomUUID()` and stored in localStorage\n\n#### **flightsSlice** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/flightsSlice.ts`)\n\n**State Interface**:\n```typescript\ninterface FlightsState {\n  flights: FlightResult[]\n  loading: boolean\n  total: number\n  page: number\n  totalPages: number\n  loadingMore: boolean\n  sortBy: SortOption  // 'best' | 'price' | 'duration' | 'departure' | 'arrival'\n  stopsFilter: StopsFilter  // nonstop, oneStop, twoPlusStops\n  airlinesFilter: string[]\n  priceRange: [number, number]\n  priceRangeMax: [number, number]\n  durationRange: [number, number]\n  durationRangeMax: [number, number]\n  departureTimeFilter: TimeFilter\n  arrivalTimeFilter: TimeFilter\n  expandedLegs: Record<string, FlightLeg[]>\n  expandedLegsLoading: Record<string, boolean>\n  isTracked: boolean\n  isTrackedLoading: boolean\n}\n```\n\n**Key Actions**:\n- `setSortBy` - Changes sort order\n- `setStopsFilter`, `setAirlinesFilter` - Updates filter selections\n- `setPriceRange`, `setDurationRange` - Sets range filters\n- `setDepartureTimeFilter`, `setArrivalTimeFilter` - Sets time filters\n- `resetFilters` - Clears all filters\n\n**Async Thunks** (Price Tracking Related):\n- `checkTrackedRoute` - Checks if a route is currently tracked for session\n  - Query params: `session`, `origin`, `destination`\n  - Returns: `{ tracked: boolean }`\n  \n- `toggleTrackRoute` - Enables/disables price tracking for a route\n  - Params:\n    - `sessionToken`\n    - `originCode`, `destCode`\n    - `departureDateStart`, `departureDateEnd`, `cabinClass` (optional)\n    - `isCurrentlyTracked` - Determines if DELETE or POST request\n  - DELETE: Removes route from tracked_routes\n  - POST: Adds route to tracked_routes with date range and cabin class\n\n**Other Async Thunks**:\n- `searchFlights` - Searches flights with pagination\n- `loadMoreFlights` - Loads additional results\n- `fetchFlightLegs` - Gets detailed leg information for a flight\n\n### 9. Related Components\n\n**Component Structure**:\n\n**Search Form Components**:\n- `TripTypeSelector` - Custom dropdown for trip type selection\n- `PassengerCountSelector` - Dropdown with +/- buttons for passenger counts\n- `CabinClassSelector` - Dropdown for cabin class selection\n- `AirportAutocomplete` - Autocomplete input with API-driven suggestions\n- `DatePicker` - Calendar-based date picker\n- `SearchButton` - Initiates flight search\n\n**Results Page Components**:\n- `SearchSummaryBar` - Shows and allows editing of search parameters\n- `TrackPricesToggle` - Toggle for price tracking\n- `FilterSidebar` - Filter options (stops, airlines, price, duration, time)\n- `FlightResultCard` - Individual flight result display\n- `Pagination` - \"Load more\" button for additional results\n\n**Other Pages**:\n- `SearchPage` - Home page with search form\n- `SearchResultsPage` - Results display page\n- `MyTripsPage` - User's trips and tracked routes\n- `FlightDetailsPage` - Detailed flight information\n- `ExplorePage` - Explore destinations\n\n**Styling**: Each component has a corresponding `.css` file with BEM-like class naming\n\n### 10. Key Project Dependencies\n\n- **React 18.3.1** - UI framework\n- **Redux Toolkit 2.5.0** - State management\n- **React Redux 9.2.0** - React-Redux bindings\n- **React Router DOM 7.1.1** - Routing\n- **Playwright 1.49.1** - E2E testing with Replay.io integration\n- **TypeScript 5.7.2** - Type safety\n- **Vite 6.0.5** - Build tool\n- **Netlify Functions** - Serverless backend\n\nThis comprehensive exploration reveals a well-structured React/Redux application with extensive Playwright-based test coverage, Redux state management for search and flights tracking, and inline editing capabilities in the SearchSummaryBar component paired with price tracking functionality via TrackPricesToggle."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a4ef7c60ae09794f5 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 50113\ntool_uses: 28\nduration_ms: 83605</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"749045d3-bc8c-40ae-9c1b-d62b27286993","uuid":"21ecfb2f-08f6-4926-a349-b7c3292dc61e","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the google-flights app in /repo/apps/. Find:\n1. The app directory name\n2. The test files that already exist (*.spec.ts)\n3. The docs/tests.md file with test specifications\n4. The SearchSummaryBar component and related components\n5. The TrackPricesToggle component\n6. The playwright config\n7. Any existing test helpers or fixtures\n8. The Redux store/slices related to search and tracking\n\nBe thorough - read the test spec entries for SearchSummaryBar and TrackPricesToggle specifically.","agentId":"a4ef7c60ae09794f5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Google Flights App - Complete Exploration Summary\n\n### 1. App Directory Name\n- **Location**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights`\n\n### 2. Test Files (*.spec.ts)\nLocated in `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/`:\n- `airport-autocomplete.spec.ts`\n- `cabin-class-selector.spec.ts`\n- `date-picker.spec.ts`\n- `passenger-count-selector.spec.ts`\n- `popular-destinations.spec.ts`\n- `recent-searches.spec.ts`\n- `search-button.spec.ts`\n- `trip-type-selector.spec.ts`\n\n### 3. Test Documentation\n- **File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/docs/tests.md`\n- **Content**: Comprehensive test specifications for all components across the application\n\n### 4. SearchSummaryBar Component\n\n**Location**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/SearchSummaryBar.tsx`\n\n**Purpose**: Displays search parameters on the results page and allows inline editing of each parameter.\n\n**Props Interface**:\n```typescript\ninterface SearchSummaryBarProps {\n  origin: string\n  destination: string\n  departureDate: string\n  returnDate: string | null\n  tripType: string\n  cabinClass: string\n  adults: number\n  children: number\n  infants: number\n  onSearch: (params: {...}) => void\n}\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Displays origin, destination, dates (single or range), passenger count, and cabin class as clickable chips\n- Inline editing with dropdown/autocomplete editors for each chip\n- Click-outside detection to close editors without changes\n- Uses component state to track which field is being edited\n- Related components: `AirportAutocomplete`, `DatePicker`, `PassengerCountSelector`, `CabinClassSelector`\n\n**Test Specifications** (from docs/tests.md):\n1. **SearchSummaryBar displays search parameters after search** - Shows all parameters (LAX → JFK, dates, passengers, cabin class) inline and clickable\n2. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit origin airport** - Click origin, autocomplete editor opens, type and select airport, search re-executes\n3. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit destination airport** - Click destination, editor opens, select new airport, results update\n4. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit departure date** - Click departure date, date picker opens, select new date, search re-executes\n5. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit return date** - Click return date, date picker opens, select new date for round trip\n6. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit passengers** - Click passenger count, selector opens, adjust counts (adults/children/infants)\n7. **SearchSummaryBar inline edit cabin class** - Click cabin class, dropdown shows options (Economy, Premium Economy, Business, First), selection triggers re-search\n8. **SearchSummaryBar inline editor closes without changes on outside click** - Clicking outside editor closes it without updating parameters\n9. **SearchSummaryBar can be edited multiple times in sequence** - Each edit triggers a new search; summary reflects all changes\n\n### 5. TrackPricesToggle Component\n\n**Location**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TrackPricesToggle.tsx`\n\n**Purpose**: Toggle button to enable/disable price tracking for a specific flight route.\n\n**Props Interface**:\n```typescript\ninterface TrackPricesToggleProps {\n  originCode: string\n  destCode: string\n  departureDate: string\n  returnDate: string | null\n  cabinClass: string\n}\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Displays toggle button with icon (🔔 when tracked, 🔕 when not)\n- Button text changes: \"Tracking prices\" (on) / \"Track prices\" (off)\n- Dispatches `toggleTrackRoute` Redux action from `flightsSlice`\n- Reads `isTracked` and `isTrackedLoading` from Redux state\n- Uses session token from `searchSlice`\n- Handles loading state during API calls\n\n**Test Specifications** (from docs/tests.md):\n1. **TrackPricesToggle is displayed on results page** - \"Track prices\" toggle visible, initially in off/untracked state\n2. **TrackPricesToggle enables price tracking** - Toggle switches to on state, route saved to database for session\n3. **TrackPricesToggle disables price tracking** - Toggle switches to off state, route removed from tracked_routes database\n4. **TrackPricesToggle reflects existing tracked route** - If route previously tracked, toggle shows on state when user searches same route again\n5. **TrackPricesToggle tracked route appears in My Trips** - Tracked route appears in \"Tracked\" tab of My Trips page with details\n6. **TrackPricesToggle can be toggled multiple times** - Multiple toggles work correctly; database updates on each toggle\n\n### 6. Playwright Configuration\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/playwright.config.ts`\n\n**Key Settings**:\n- **Test directory**: `./tests`\n- **Timeout**: 60 seconds per test\n- **Assertion timeout**: 10 seconds\n- **Parallel execution**: Disabled (fullyParallel: false)\n- **Workers**: 1\n- **Retries**: 0\n- **Reporter**: List format and JSON output to `test-results/results.json`\n- **Base URL**: `http://localhost:8888`\n- **Tracing**: on-first-retry\n- **Browser**: Replay-enabled Chromium\n- **Web Server**: Netlify dev server on port 8888\n\n### 7. Test Helpers and Fixtures\n\n**Location**: Inline in test files (example from `search-button.spec.ts`)\n\n**Key Helper Function**: `fillSearchForm()`\n- Fills a valid search form with origin, destination, and dates\n- Options support:\n  - `skipOrigin`, `skipDestination`, `skipDepartureDate`, `skipReturnDate`\n  - `oneWay` flag to select One Way trip type\n- Uses test IDs to interact with form fields\n- Includes error handling and wait conditions (e.g., waiting for dropdowns)\n- Example: Types airport codes (LAX for Los Angeles, JFK for New York), selects from suggestions\n\n**Pattern Used**: Test IDs follow naming convention like:\n- `trip-type-selector-trigger`\n- `origin-input`, `origin-dropdown`, `origin-suggestion-{CODE}`\n- `departure-date-trigger`, `departure-date-calendar`\n\n### 8. Redux Store/Slices\n\n**Store Location**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/store.ts`\n\n**Configured Reducers**:\n- `search` - searchSlice reducer\n- `flights` - flightsSlice reducer\n- `booking` - bookingSlice reducer\n- `trips` - tripsSlice reducer\n- `explore` - exploreSlice reducer\n\n#### **searchSlice** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/searchSlice.ts`)\n\n**State Interface**:\n```typescript\ninterface SearchState {\n  tripType: TripType  // 'round_trip' | 'one_way' | 'multi_city'\n  passengers: { adults: number; children: number; infants: number }\n  cabinClass: CabinClass  // 'economy' | 'premium_economy' | 'business' | 'first'\n  origin: Airport | null\n  destination: Airport | null\n  departureDate: string | null\n  returnDate: string | null\n  recentSearches: RecentSearch[]\n  recentSearchesLoading: boolean\n  popularDestinations: PopularDestination[]\n  popularDestinationsLoading: boolean\n  sessionToken: string\n  validationErrors: Record<string, string>\n}\n```\n\n**Key Actions**:\n- `setTripType` - Updates trip type; clears returnDate if one_way\n- `setPassengers` - Updates passenger counts\n- `setCabinClass` - Updates cabin class\n- `setOrigin`, `setDestination` - Sets airport; clears validation errors\n- `swapAirports` - Exchanges origin and destination\n- `setDepartureDate`, `setReturnDate` - Sets dates; clears validation errors\n- `setValidationErrors`, `clearValidationErrors` - Manages validation state\n\n**Async Thunks**:\n- `fetchRecentSearches` - Fetches recent searches for session\n- `saveRecentSearch` - Saves a new search\n- `fetchPopularDestinations` - Fetches popular destinations\n\n**Session Management**:\n- `sessionToken` is auto-generated with `crypto.randomUUID()` and stored in localStorage\n\n#### **flightsSlice** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/flightsSlice.ts`)\n\n**State Interface**:\n```typescript\ninterface FlightsState {\n  flights: FlightResult[]\n  loading: boolean\n  total: number\n  page: number\n  totalPages: number\n  loadingMore: boolean\n  sortBy: SortOption  // 'best' | 'price' | 'duration' | 'departure' | 'arrival'\n  stopsFilter: StopsFilter  // nonstop, oneStop, twoPlusStops\n  airlinesFilter: string[]\n  priceRange: [number, number]\n  priceRangeMax: [number, number]\n  durationRange: [number, number]\n  durationRangeMax: [number, number]\n  departureTimeFilter: TimeFilter\n  arrivalTimeFilter: TimeFilter\n  expandedLegs: Record<string, FlightLeg[]>\n  expandedLegsLoading: Record<string, boolean>\n  isTracked: boolean\n  isTrackedLoading: boolean\n}\n```\n\n**Key Actions**:\n- `setSortBy` - Changes sort order\n- `setStopsFilter`, `setAirlinesFilter` - Updates filter selections\n- `setPriceRange`, `setDurationRange` - Sets range filters\n- `setDepartureTimeFilter`, `setArrivalTimeFilter` - Sets time filters\n- `resetFilters` - Clears all filters\n\n**Async Thunks** (Price Tracking Related):\n- `checkTrackedRoute` - Checks if a route is currently tracked for session\n  - Query params: `session`, `origin`, `destination`\n  - Returns: `{ tracked: boolean }`\n  \n- `toggleTrackRoute` - Enables/disables price tracking for a route\n  - Params:\n    - `sessionToken`\n    - `originCode`, `destCode`\n    - `departureDateStart`, `departureDateEnd`, `cabinClass` (optional)\n    - `isCurrentlyTracked` - Determines if DELETE or POST request\n  - DELETE: Removes route from tracked_routes\n  - POST: Adds route to tracked_routes with date range and cabin class\n\n**Other Async Thunks**:\n- `searchFlights` - Searches flights with pagination\n- `loadMoreFlights` - Loads additional results\n- `fetchFlightLegs` - Gets detailed leg information for a flight\n\n### 9. Related Components\n\n**Component Structure**:\n\n**Search Form Components**:\n- `TripTypeSelector` - Custom dropdown for trip type selection\n- `PassengerCountSelector` - Dropdown with +/- buttons for passenger counts\n- `CabinClassSelector` - Dropdown for cabin class selection\n- `AirportAutocomplete` - Autocomplete input with API-driven suggestions\n- `DatePicker` - Calendar-based date picker\n- `SearchButton` - Initiates flight search\n\n**Results Page Components**:\n- `SearchSummaryBar` - Shows and allows editing of search parameters\n- `TrackPricesToggle` - Toggle for price tracking\n- `FilterSidebar` - Filter options (stops, airlines, price, duration, time)\n- `FlightResultCard` - Individual flight result display\n- `Pagination` - \"Load more\" button for additional results\n\n**Other Pages**:\n- `SearchPage` - Home page with search form\n- `SearchResultsPage` - Results display page\n- `MyTripsPage` - User's trips and tracked routes\n- `FlightDetailsPage` - Detailed flight information\n- `ExplorePage` - Explore destinations\n\n**Styling**: Each component has a corresponding `.css` file with BEM-like class naming\n\n### 10. Key Project Dependencies\n\n- **React 18.3.1** - UI framework\n- **Redux Toolkit 2.5.0** - State management\n- **React Redux 9.2.0** - React-Redux bindings\n- **React Router DOM 7.1.1** - Routing\n- **Playwright 1.49.1** - E2E testing with Replay.io integration\n- **TypeScript 5.7.2** - Type safety\n- **Vite 6.0.5** - Build tool\n- **Netlify Functions** - Serverless backend\n\nThis comprehensive exploration reveals a well-structured React/Redux application with extensive Playwright-based test coverage, Redux state management for search and flights tracking, and inline editing capabilities in the SearchSummaryBar component paired with price tracking functionality via TrackPricesToggle."}],"totalDurationMs":83605,"totalTokens":50113,"totalToolUseCount":28,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":764,"cache_read_input_tokens":46156,"output_tokens":3193,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":764},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
