rn date picker is hidden. The dropdown closes.\n    34→    34→\n    35→    35→#### Test: TripTypeSelector selects \"Multi-city\" option\n    36→    36→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    37→    37→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded with \"Round trip\" selected\n    38→    38→- **Action**: User clicks the trip type selector and selects \"Multi-city\"\n    39→    39→- **Expected**: The selector updates to show \"Multi-city\". The search form adjusts to support multi-city input (multiple origin/destination pairs).\n    40→    40→\n    41→    41→#### Test: TripTypeSelector switches back to \"Round trip\" from \"One way\"\n    42→    42→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector, DatePicker\n    43→    43→- **Initial state**: \"One way\" is currently selected, return date picker is hidden\n    44→    44→- **Action**: User clicks the trip type selector and selects \"Round trip\"\n    45→    45→- **Expected**: The selector updates to show \"Round trip\". The return date picker becomes visible again.\n    46→    46→\n    47→    47→#### Test: TripTypeSelector closes dropdown when clicking outside\n    48→    48→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    49→    49→- **Initial state**: Trip type dropdown is open\n    50→    50→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown\n    51→    51→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes without changing the selection.\n    52→    52→\n    53→    53→#### Test: TripTypeSelector can be used multiple times in sequence\n    54→    54→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    55→    55→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded with default \"Round trip\"\n    56→    56→- **Action**: User selects \"One way\", then interacts with another element (e.g., clicks airport field), then opens the trip type selector again and selects \"Round trip\"\n    57→    57→- **Expected**: Each interaction correctly updates the selector. The dropdown opens and closes properly on each use. The final state shows \"Round trip\" selected.\n    58→    58→\n    59→    59→### PassengerCountSelector\n    60→    60→\n    61→    61→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector displays default \"1 Adult\"\n    62→    62→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    63→    63→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with default settings\n    64→    64→- **Action**: User observes the passenger count selector\n    65→    65→- **Expected**: The selector displays \"1\" or \"1 Adult\" as the default.\n    66→    66→\n    67→    67→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector opens dropdown with passenger categories\n    68→    68→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    69→    69→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, passenger selector is closed\n    70→    70→- **Action**: User clicks the passenger count selector\n    71→    71→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing three categories: Adults, Children, and Infants. Each category has a label, a current count, and \"+\" and \"−\" buttons.\n    72→    72→\n    73→    73→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments adult count\n    74→    74→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    75→    75→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults count is 1\n    76→    76→- **Action**: User clicks the \"+\" button next to Adults\n    77→    77→- **Expected**: Adults count increases to 2. The selector label updates to reflect the new total (e.g., \"2 passengers\" or \"2 Adults\").\n    78→    78→\n    79→    79→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector decrements adult count with minimum of 1\n    80→    80→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    81→    81→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults count is 1\n    82→    82→- **Action**: User clicks the \"−\" button next to Adults\n    83→    83→- **Expected**: Adults count remains at 1. The \"−\" button is disabled or has no effect since at least 1 adult is required.\n    84→    84→\n    85→    85→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments and decrements children\n    86→    86→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    87→    87→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Children count is 0\n    88→    88→- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Children twice, then clicks \"−\" once\n    89→    89→- **Expected**: Children count goes to 1. The total passenger display updates accordingly.\n    90→    90→\n    91→    91→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments and decrements infants\n    92→    92→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    93→    93→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Infants count is 0\n    94→    94→- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Infants\n    95→    95→- **Expected**: Infants count increases to 1. The total passenger display updates accordingly.\n    96→    96→\n    97→    97→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector prevents infants exceeding adults\n    98→    98→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    99→    99→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults = 1, Infants = 1\n   100→   100→- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Infants\n   101→   101→- **Expected**: Infants count remains at 1 (cannot exceed number of adults). The \"+\" button is disabled or has no effect.\n   102→   102→\n   103→   103→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector closes dropdown and retains values\n   104→   104→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n   105→   105→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults = 2, Children = 1, Infants = 0\n   106→   106→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown to close it\n   107→   107→- **Expected**: Dropdown closes. The selector label shows the updated total (e.g., \"3 passengers\"). Reopening the dropdown shows the same values (2 Adults, 1 Child, 0 Infants).\n   108→   108→\n   109→   109→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector can be used repeatedly\n   110→   110→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n   111→   111→- **Initial state**: Search page with default passenger counts\n   112→   112→- **Action**: User opens the selector, adds 1 adult, closes it, interacts with another element (e.g., selects cabin class), then reopens the passenger selector and adds 1 child\n   113→   113→- **Expected**: All values persist correctly between opens. Final state shows 2 Adults, 1 Child. The selector works correctly on each subsequent use.\n   114→   114→\n   115→   115→### CabinClassSelector\n   116→   116→\n   117→   117→#### Test: CabinClassSelector displays default \"Economy\"\n   118→   118→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   119→   119→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with default settings\n   120→   120→- **Action**: User observes the cabin class selector\n   121→   121→- **Expected**: The selector displays \"Economy\" as the default selected cabin class. It is rendered as a custom dropdown.\n   122→   122→\n   123→   123→#### Test: CabinClassSelector opens dropdown showing all cabin classes\n   124→   124→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   125→   125→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, cabin class selector is closed\n   126→   126→- **Action**: User clicks the cabin class selector\n   127→   127→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing four options: \"Economy\", \"Premium Economy\", \"Business\", and \"First\".\n   128→   128→\n   129→   129→#### Test: CabinClassSelector selects \"Business\" class\n   130→   130→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   131→   131→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open with \"Economy\" selected\n   132→   132→- **Action**: User clicks \"Business\"\n   133→   133→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The selector label updates to \"Business\".\n   134→   134→\n   135→   135→#### Test: CabinClassSelector selects \"Premium Economy\" class\n   136→   136→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   137→   137→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open\n   138→   138→- **Action**: User clicks \"Premium Economy\"\n   139→   139→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The selector label updates to \"Premium Economy\".\n   140→   140→\n   141→   141→#### Test: CabinClassSelector selects \"First\" class\n   142→   142→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   143→   143→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open\n   144→   144→- **Action**: User clicks \"First\"\n   145→   145→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The selector label updates to \"First\".\n   146→   146→\n   147→   147→#### Test: CabinClassSelector closes dropdown when clicking outside\n   148→   148→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   149→   149→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open\n   150→   150→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown\n   151→   151→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes without changing the selection.\n   152→   152→\n   153→   153→#### Test: CabinClassSelector can be changed multiple times\n   154→   154→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   155→   155→- **Initial state**: Search page with \"Economy\" selected\n   156→   156→- **Action**: User selects \"Business\", interacts with another element, then reopens and selects \"First\", then reopens and selects \"Economy\"\n   157→   157→- **Expected**: Each selection correctly updates the label. The final state shows \"Economy\". The dropdown works correctly on each use.\n   158→   158→\n   159→   159→### AirportAutocomplete\n   160→   160→\n   161→   161→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete origin field shows placeholder text\n   162→   162→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   163→   163→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with empty origin field\n   164→   164→- **Action**: User observes the origin airport field\n   165→   165→- **Expected**: The field displays placeholder text indicating the user should enter an origin (e.g., \"Where from?\").\n   166→   166→\n   167→   167→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete destination field shows placeholder text\n   168→   168→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   169→   169→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with empty destination field\n   170→   170→- **Action**: User observes the destination airport field\n   171→   171→- **Expected**: The field displays placeholder text indicat